      "text": "Risk-limit monitoring must distinguish entry inhibition, temporary protection locks and broader trading halts. Freqtrade documents pair and side scope, expiry, closed-trade drawdown calculations and continued handling of open trades during entry pauses. Repository examples add explicit kill-switch status, preflight checks and restart latches. Vendor guidance recommends separate exposure, daily-loss, cumulative-drawdown and volatility controls, with a defined response and restart policy. Stop-order execution limitations and simulation timing differences constrain what a configured threshold proves. These findings support checking the specific control and its documented semantics rather than treating a single stopped/running label as sufficient.",
